{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1413084085,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU4NzcyMjMy","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/8#issuecomment-58772232"},"message":"Here is some further information from sent out email\n\n```\n$\u003e wget -q -O- http://openfmri.s3.amazonaws.com/\\?versions\\\u0026prefix\\=ds105/sub001/BOLD/task001_run001/bold.nii.gz | xmllint --format -\n\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?\u003e\n\u003cListVersionsResult xmlns=\"http://s3.amazonaws.com/doc/2006-03-01/\"\u003e\n  \u003cName\u003eopenfmri\u003c/Name\u003e\n  \u003cPrefix\u003eds105/sub001/BOLD/task001_run001/bold.nii.gz\u003c/Prefix\u003e\n  \u003cKeyMarker/\u003e\n  \u003cVersionIdMarker/\u003e\n  \u003cMaxKeys\u003e1000\u003c/MaxKeys\u003e\n  \u003cIsTruncated\u003efalse\u003c/IsTruncated\u003e\n  \u003cVersion\u003e\n    \u003cKey\u003eds105/sub001/BOLD/task001_run001/bold.nii.gz\u003c/Key\u003e\n    \u003cVersionId\u003enull\u003c/VersionId\u003e\n    \u003cIsLatest\u003etrue\u003c/IsLatest\u003e\n    \u003cLastModified\u003e2014-05-28T16:35:55.000Z\u003c/LastModified\u003e\n    \u003cETag\u003e\"c4bcd589d59ab718fb952dc503db99f6-4\"\u003c/ETag\u003e\n    \u003cSize\u003e25433569\u003c/Size\u003e\n    \u003cStorageClass\u003eSTANDARD\u003c/StorageClass\u003e\n  \u003c/Version\u003e\n\u003c/ListVersionsResult\u003e\n```\n\nlook at the ETag:\n\n```\n    \u003cETag\u003e\"c4bcd589d59ab718fb952dc503db99f6-4\"\u003c/ETag\u003e\n```\n\nusually, for non \"chunk\"ed uploads, ETag simply corresponds to the md5 sum of\nthat file, which makes it easy to reliably reference it out based on md5sum of\nthe file at hands.  With \"parallel\" upload I guess chunking is used, then ETag\nis computed as a md5sum of the concatenated md5sums for each chunk, which makes\n\"de-referencing\" more difficult.\n\nUpon a quick search,  for \"small\" files under 5GB it is easy to cause md5sum recomputation:\nhttp://stackoverflow.com/a/19033497/1265472\n\n```\n    We're currently doing an ugly (but so far useful) hack to fix those wrong ETags in multipart uploaded files, which consists on applying a change to the file in the bucket; that triggers a md5 recalculation from Amazon that changes the ETag to ma\ntches with the actual md5 signature.\n\n    In our case:\n\n    File: bucket/Foo.mpg.gpg\n\n        ETag obtained: \"3f92dffef0a11d175e60fb8b958b4e6e-2\"\n        Do something with the file (rename it, add a meta-data like a fake header, among others)\n        Etag obtained: \"c1d903ca1bb6dc68778ef21e74cc15b0\"\n\n    We don't know the algorithm, but since we can \"fix\" the ETag we don't need to worry about it either.\n```","files":null}]}